WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.419 --> 00:00:04.752
- I grew up in the family of skywriting.

00:00:06.041 --> 00:00:08.123
I was just a little
kid, that's all I knew.

00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:11.973
Just like being an artist of the sky.

00:00:11.973 --> 00:00:15.483
I'm Greg Stinis, and I own
a company called SkyTypers

00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:17.691
with my son, Stephen Stinis.

00:00:17.691 --> 00:00:20.108
(calm music)

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:31.133
My dad was one of the original skywriters.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.716
He started in 1931.

00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:36.469
And one airplane travels a big circle

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.655
if he's gonna make an “o”

00:00:37.655 --> 00:00:40.035
and that takes a lot of time to do that.

00:00:40.035 --> 00:00:42.748
And he decided, "Hey,
there's gotta be a faster way

00:00:42.748 --> 00:00:43.967
"to do this.

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:46.267
"I'll just do it with
a bunch of airplanes."

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:50.431
And so he came up with
the method of skytyping:

00:00:50.431 --> 00:00:53.039
five airplanes flying in formation.

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:55.273
For instance, if we're gonna make an “i,”

00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:57.447
everybody lets out just one puff.

00:00:57.447 --> 00:00:58.551
There's your “i.”

00:00:58.551 --> 00:01:01.771
If you wanna turn that
into an “l,” it's one puff,

00:01:01.771 --> 00:01:04.412
plus the bottom guy lets
out three more puffs.

00:01:04.412 --> 00:01:05.662
There's your “l.”

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:12.249
This is a very specialized form of flying.

00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:15.825
Most of my pilots have got
like 10,000 flying hours,

00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:18.158
so they're very experienced.

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:21.350
We fly AA-5B Tiger planes.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.889
When we fly, it's roughly 45
minutes to get up to altitude,

00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:29.639
which is 10,000 feet.

00:01:30.948 --> 00:01:35.115
A typical skytyping message is
20 characters, sometimes 25,

00:01:35.985 --> 00:01:39.341
and that's roughly five miles in length.

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:41.886
Each letter is the size of
the Empire State Building,

00:01:41.886 --> 00:01:43.219
1,200 feet tall.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.760
They're the biggest ads in the world

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.024
and you can't miss them.

00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:50.107
The whole sky becomes your billboard.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.340
(airplane starting)

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.973
I do this 'cause not only is it fun,

00:01:57.973 --> 00:01:59.157
'cause I love flying,

00:01:59.157 --> 00:02:02.435
but I like the
accomplishment of what we do,

00:02:02.435 --> 00:02:04.367
'cause the people we fly for,

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.117
they're all thrilled.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:10.025
We've gotten something like
120 years of skywriting

00:02:10.025 --> 00:02:11.192
in the family.

00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:16.168
My dad trained me, and I've trained my son,

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:19.668
and I'm very proud about the whole thing.

